requirements_text:
Applicants must be over 18 years of age, be proficient in French or English, and reside in South Africa, Benin, Cameroon, Ghana, Guinea, Kenya, Mali, Mozambique, Uganda, the Republic of the Congo, Rwanda or Senegal.
Be a journalist, communications professional, content creator, influencer or media host/presenter;
Be over 18 years old;
Have between two and five years of professional experience in communications, journalism, media or content creation;
Demonstrate a strong interest in performing arts, music and, more broadly, the cultural and creative industries;
Have an active audience and a demonstrated local presence (social media, local media outlet, community, etc.);
Reside in one of the 12 countries covered by the scheme: South Africa, Benin, Cameroon, Ghana, Guinea, Kenya, Mali, Mozambique, Uganda, Republic of the Congo, Rwanda or Senegal.
Fluency in French or English is mandatory.
Applicants must be permanent residents of sub-Saharan Africa, be at least 18 years old, and be affiliated with an organization that has had legal status for at least one year.
The mentoring program is destined for professionals in the performing arts and music industries, in early career (2 to 5 years of experience required) and living and working in sub-Saharan Africa.
Agé·es de plus de 18 ans et sans limite d’âge, les candidat·es devront justifier de deux à cinq ans d’expérience professionnelle dans les métiers d’accompagnement du spectacle vivant ou des musiques.

